        "content": [
          {
            "type": "output_text",
            "text": "**No results on O'Reilly (oreilly.com).**[[1]](https://www.baseten.co/inference-engineering/)\n\nThe book *Inference Engineering* by Philip Kiely exists but is published by **Baseten Books** (not O'Reilly). It is described as a guide to the hardware, software, techniques, and infrastructure for running AI models in production, covering topics like CUDA, Kubernetes, and optimizing generative AI deployment.[[1]](https://www.baseten.co/inference-engineering/)\n\n- It launched recently (around early 2026) and is available as a digital download or physical book via Baseten\u2019s site: [baseten.co/inference-engineering](https://www.baseten.co/inference-engineering/).[[1]](https://www.baseten.co/inference-engineering/)\n- It has received positive mentions from figures like Sarah Guo, Scott Hanselman, and Lenny Rachitsky.[[1]](https://www.baseten.co/inference-engineering/)\n- It is sometimes referred to as a free or democratizing textbook/resource on the topic.[[2]](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/michael-gribben_a-quote-from-jonathon-belotti-that-resonated-activity-7460412549486862336-JnV7)\n\nSearches restricted to `site:oreilly.com` (including variations like \u201cO Reilly\u201d) returned no matching book or author listings. A related but unrelated tweet mentioned other O'Reilly titles in passing.[[3]](https://x.com/amritwt/status/2082208055345959076)\n\nIf you're looking for O'Reilly titles on similar topics (e.g., AI inference, MLOps, or production ML), their catalog has many options\u2014let me know for recommendations!",
